Nexo's patches to Mupen64Plus-Next (libretro/mupen64plus-libretro-nx @ 15bada85906593376e8fd697f1b0b3af3a20f512)
for its WebAssembly build (../build.sh). Everything new is under NEXO_REENTRANT / NEXO=1, so the patched tree
still builds the upstream way for other platforms.

- cached_interp.c, r4300_core.c, main.c: no libco in WebAssembly. The cached interpreter returns at every VI
  (nexo_co_yield, set by the frontend's co_switch(retro_thread)) and nexo_resume_emulation() continues it from the
  same PC on the next retro_run(). Makefile.common: libco.c isn't built (the frontend provides co_*).
- emulate_game_controller_via_libretro.c: the controller state (buttons + stick, already mapped to the N64 pad)
  comes straight from the frontend (nexo_n64_keys) instead of going through a RetroPad.
- ai_controller.c: AI_DRAM_ADDR is 24 bits wide, as on hardware (homebrew writes KSEG1 addresses there; kept as is
  they index far outside RDRAM).
- memory.c: the compressed memory layout (~12 MB) instead of a 512 MB block that only simplifies dynarec address
  arithmetic.
- Makefile: no -fcommon (WebAssembly objects have no common symbols: tentative definitions would stay undefined).
- xxhash.h: no NEON-via-SIMDe header (it can't be included inside xxhash's extern "C"): scalar XXH3.
- atomicops.h: no sem_timedwait without threads (only the threaded renderer, which is off, waits on it).

